{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bitesofbostonfoodtours/items/151824/", "pk": 151824, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bitesofbostonfoodtours/", "pk": 31501, "shortname": "bitesofbostonfoodtours", "name": "Bites of Boston Food Tours", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "A Taste of the Freedom Trail", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 9, "unicode": "A Taste of the Freedom Trail", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": true, "sold_out_text": "SOLD OUT!", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-midnight", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 26.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 1.5, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": true, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 1500, "description": "#The perfect introduction to everything Boston!\n\n*Sample and learn about iconic dishes as you’re treated to the city’s best spots for Lobster Rolls, New England Clam Chowder, Boston Baked Beans and Boston Cream Pie.*\n\n-----", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "Downtown / Freedom Trail / Faneuil Hall", "booking_notes": "## Important Details / What to Bring\n\n* **Please arrive at least 10 minutes early, as our tours start right on time**.\n* Please **bring bottled water** along with you to enjoy throughout the tour. Beverages are not included with all food tastings.\n* If you are consuming alcohol, please bring your **driver's license or passport!**\n* Gratuity for your tour guide is *not included in your ticket price*. While not mandatory, if you enjoy yourself and would like to consider a tip for your tour guide, **gratuities are greatly appreciated and graciously accepted at the end of the tour.**\n* This tour takes place rain or shine and New England weather can be unpredictable, so **please check the weather and temperature on the day of your tour and dress for the forecast**. We have fun in all types of weather, and being prepared for the elements will go a long way in making the most of your tour experience!\n* **Please wear comfortable clothes and walking shoes. We will be outdoors and on our feet for most of the tour**, and we want you to be as comfortable as possible.\n* Taking photos is welcomed encouraged!\n___________________________________\n## Parking\n\n**Parking can be difficult and expensive in Boston. Whenever possible, arriving via the T or by taxi / Uber/ Lyft is the best option.**\n\nThe Beantown Pub can be reached via the MBTA on the following lines:\nRed and Green Lines (subway): Park Street T stop\nOrange and Blue Lines (subway): State T stop\n\nThere are many parking lots and garages within close proximity to the Meeting Location. Here are 2 suggested options:\n\n*Pi Alley Parking Garage*\nParking Garage\n275 Washington St\nBoston, MA 02108\nOpen 24 hours\n\n*Boston Common Garage*\nParking Garage\n0 Charles Street\nBoston, MA, 02116\nOpen 24 hours\n\n\nMost metered parking in the neighborhood has a 2-hour limit, which will not be enough for the duration of the tour. Also, please always be sure to read all posted signs and notices regarding resident-only parking, street-cleaning, handicapped spots, commercial zones, time limits, etc.. Parking rules are strictly enforced in Boston! \n___________________________________\n## Other FAQs\n\n**How much food can I expect to eat during the tour?**\nWe provide tastings, so please do not expect a full meal at each location. Tastings vary in portion size, with some tastings served while seated inside the restaurant, and others served in a more “on the go” manner to also allow time for the neighborhood component of the tour.\n\n**Can children participate in the tour? What about toddlers and strollers?**\nChildren ages 12 and older are welcome to participate. This activity is not appropriate to attend with infants and, due to space limitations, strollers are not permitted on any of our tours.\n\n**Are restrooms available during the tour?**\nRestrooms will be available at the beginning and end of the tour at the corresponding tasting locations.", "cancellation_notes": "**For Non-Refundable Tickets:** All sales are final - no refunds or exchanges.\n\n**For Refundable Tickets:** At least 48 hours notice is required in order to receive a refund. Tickets canceled less than 48 hours prior to the tour start time will not be refunded or rescheduled. Late arrivals and / or No-shows will also not be refunded or rescheduled. Thank you for your cooperation.\n\n*PLEASE CHECK YOUR EVENT DATE CAREFULLY BEFORE BOOKING.*\n\nThis experience was created as an adult activity. **We kindly ask that all guests joining our tour be at least 12 years of age.** This activity is not appropriate to attend with infants or toddlers, and strollers are not permitted on any of our tours.\n\nDue to agreements in place with our partner restaurants, there is a maximum guest capacity per tour. **EVERY participant must have a ticket to join the tour.**", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "Iconic Boston Food & History Tour", "short_description": "", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/Z6ATZ2VTpPM64Vi1SD7Q", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/Z6ATZ2VTpPM64Vi1SD7Q", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bitesofbostonfoodtours/items/151824/images/1148844/", "pk": 1148844, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestack